00:03:25.115 --> 00:03:26.198
The real you.

00:03:27.708 --> 00:03:28.875
The truth you.

00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:31.075
- Wow!

00:03:32.802 --> 00:03:34.618
Nina's excited, look at that.

00:03:34.618 --> 00:03:37.310
- It's overwhelming, but it's good.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:38.846
I feel good.

00:03:38.846 --> 00:03:40.077
There's a lot of stuff

00:03:40.077 --> 00:03:43.505
that you won't expect
to take from this event.

00:03:43.505 --> 00:03:45.172
I was crying so much

00:03:48.313 --> 00:03:50.935
that my mascara and my eyeliner

00:03:50.935 --> 00:03:53.062
all smudge over my face.

00:03:53.062 --> 00:03:54.474
Notes to the ladies,

00:03:54.474 --> 00:03:57.877
do not wear mascaras and eyeliners.

00:03:57.877 --> 00:03:59.381
- You can get waterproof ones.

00:03:59.381 --> 00:04:01.446
Notes to the ladies,
there's waterproof versions.

00:04:01.446 --> 00:04:02.760
- Waterproof, yeah.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.328
- Okay, I know this.

00:04:04.328 --> 00:04:05.762
I'm putting lemon on my salad.

00:04:05.762 --> 00:04:06.845
We're eating.

00:04:07.728 --> 00:04:09.684
We all got salad.

00:04:09.684 --> 00:04:11.016
Part of the end is they challenge you

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:12.296
to do a 10-day challenge

00:04:12.296 --> 00:04:15.410
of basically healthy eating of no ...

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:16.243
What can we have?

00:04:16.243 --> 00:04:17.661
No caffeine, no coff ...

00:04:17.661 --> 00:04:19.533
No caffeine, no coffee,

00:04:19.533 --> 00:04:21.200
no dairy, no sugars.

00:04:23.199 --> 00:04:24.603
- No meat.
- No meats.

00:04:24.603 --> 00:04:28.344
And what else we're not
doing anything with flour.

00:04:28.344 --> 00:04:30.198
So, it really limits
your options for 10 days.

00:04:30.198 --> 00:04:31.887
But we got salads.

00:04:31.887 --> 00:04:32.970
There's mine.

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:35.768
There's Nina's.

00:04:35.768 --> 00:04:38.183
And there's Lily's,

00:04:38.183 --> 00:04:40.956
which is a good segue over to Lily.

00:04:40.956 --> 00:04:43.086
How was your experience, Lily?

00:04:43.086 --> 00:04:45.132
- It was outstanding.

00:04:45.132 --> 00:04:47.341
It was really good, really good.

00:04:47.341 --> 00:04:50.070
The thing that I actually really learned

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:52.840
about myself is that I was making up

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:54.602
all these stories in my head.

00:04:54.602 --> 00:04:56.030
I was letting it control me.

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:57.069
I was ...

00:04:57.069 --> 00:05:00.175
Nobody wanted to listen to my voice.

00:05:00.175 --> 00:05:04.032
People didn't want to hear my message.

00:05:04.032 --> 00:05:05.386
Nobody cares.

00:05:05.386 --> 00:05:08.026
All that stuff and I realized

00:05:08.026 --> 00:05:11.500
it held me back from
doing a lot of things.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.147
I wanted to launch a
YouTube video, channel,

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:16.192
which I didn't do because,
I'm like, nobody wants

00:05:16.192 --> 00:05:17.454
to hear what I want to say.

00:05:17.454 --> 00:05:19.209
I have nothing important to say.

00:05:19.209 --> 00:05:21.340
I don't do well on my Snapchat videos

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.447
because nobody wants to say ...

00:05:23.447 --> 00:05:25.992
Nobody wants to know what I've got to say.

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:27.742
But more importantly,

00:05:28.602 --> 00:05:30.185
I don't help people

00:05:31.186 --> 00:05:33.958
who I think could do so much better

00:05:33.958 --> 00:05:35.888
because I assume they don't want

00:05:35.888 --> 00:05:37.148
to hear what I have to say.

00:05:37.148 --> 00:05:38.481
And as a result,

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:43.038
I allow them to be in their state

00:05:43.038 --> 00:05:46.618
and their situation and I
just watch from the sidelines.

00:05:46.618 --> 00:05:48.118
So, no more, okay?

00:05:49.487 --> 00:05:51.054
I have something to say

00:05:51.054 --> 00:05:53.188
and what it is I want to say is

00:05:53.188 --> 00:05:55.280
that I believe that every single person

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.969
have the power within them

00:05:56.969 --> 00:05:59.673
to be extraordinary and that's my message

00:05:59.673 --> 00:06:02.039
to everybody and that's
what I want to say.

00:06:02.039 --> 00:06:05.295
(people cheering)

00:06:05.295 --> 00:06:06.396
- [Evan] Deep in the dark there,

00:06:06.396 --> 00:06:09.442
we've got Alex playing the piano.

00:06:09.442 --> 00:06:10.287
Alex!

00:06:10.287 --> 00:06:11.255
- Yeah.

00:06:11.255 --> 00:06:12.364
- [Evan] I'm zooming in on you.

00:06:12.364 --> 00:06:13.667
Oh, he's coming out.

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:15.125
- [Alex] What's up?

00:06:15.125 --> 00:06:15.958
- [Evan] This is Alex.

00:06:15.958 --> 00:06:17.068
You guys know Alex.

00:06:17.068 --> 00:06:18.200
What did you take away?

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:19.033
What did you learn?

00:06:19.033 --> 00:06:20.029
What do you want to tell?

00:06:20.029 --> 00:06:21.990
- I'm going to pour myself a
drink as I tell you the story.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.564
- [Evan] All right.
- So, what did I learn?

00:06:24.564 --> 00:06:25.397
There's a lot.

00:06:25.397 --> 00:06:27.314
There's a ton of notes.

00:06:28.894 --> 00:06:30.764
Woo, Nina, you want some wine,

00:06:30.764 --> 00:06:31.642
as she takes a bottle of wine too?

00:06:31.642 --> 00:06:32.475
So, what I learned ...

00:06:32.475 --> 00:06:34.177
I lost my voice multiple times,

00:06:34.177 --> 00:06:36.727
but that didn't stop me from yelling

00:06:36.727 --> 00:06:38.310
and going full out.

00:06:39.657 --> 00:06:42.028
And, jeez, I became aware

00:06:42.028 --> 00:06:45.945
of how many limiting
beliefs I have and how ...

00:06:46.799 --> 00:06:50.382
How I've never really
been aware of myself.

00:06:51.813 --> 00:06:52.646
It's a weird thing to say.

00:06:52.646 --> 00:06:55.971
But especially in the
last day right at the end,

00:06:55.971 --> 00:06:57.154
we were supposed to have this conversation

00:06:57.154 --> 00:06:59.349
with our future self or ourselves

00:06:59.349 --> 00:07:01.253
and just recognize ourselves

00:07:01.253 --> 00:07:03.352
and I've never really done that.

00:07:03.352 --> 00:07:05.242
And it made me super emotional.

00:07:05.242 --> 00:07:06.923
I started crying.

00:07:06.923 --> 00:07:10.402
Like, I've never talked to
myself and been proud of myself.

00:07:10.402 --> 00:07:11.268
I'm finding that out

00:07:11.268 --> 00:07:13.074
as I'm continuously growing as a leader,

00:07:13.074 --> 00:07:15.262
as I'm trying to be a great role model,

00:07:15.262 --> 00:07:17.925
as I'm trying to build something amazing

00:07:17.925 --> 00:07:20.399
and have a safe place for people.

00:07:20.399 --> 00:07:22.072
I'm really hard on myself

00:07:22.072 --> 00:07:23.585
and I think that there
should be a fine balance

00:07:23.585 --> 00:07:27.612
between not being satisfied
and wanting to grow,

00:07:27.612 --> 00:07:29.405
but not feeling like a failure.

00:07:29.405 --> 00:07:31.438
And, so, for me, one of the things

00:07:31.438 --> 00:07:32.674
that was an issue a lot

00:07:32.674 --> 00:07:33.951
was I've always had trouble

00:07:33.951 --> 00:07:35.914
receiving compliments from people.

00:07:35.914 --> 00:07:37.043
Every time I'd get a compliment,

00:07:37.043 --> 00:07:38.796
in my mind, I'd be like, well,

00:07:38.796 --> 00:07:39.901
I'm still procrastinating,

00:07:39.901 --> 00:07:40.947
I'm still doing all these bad things

00:07:40.947 --> 00:07:42.009
and I don't feel I deserve.

00:07:42.009 --> 00:07:46.457
I'd feel ashamed even though
they're sharing their love.

00:07:46.457 --> 00:07:48.826
And so one of the things
that came out for me was

00:07:48.826 --> 00:07:50.836
I deserve to be proud.

00:07:50.836 --> 00:07:52.574
There's a lot of things
that I've accomplished,

00:07:52.574 --> 00:07:54.695
there's a lot of difficulties
that I went through.

00:07:54.695 --> 00:07:56.150
It's hard to realize that.

00:07:56.150 --> 00:07:59.317
That I've thought so little of myself.

00:08:01.584 --> 00:08:04.752
So that was one of the
things that I realized.

00:08:04.752 --> 00:08:06.615
There's a bunch of other things,
like I'm quitting smoking.

00:08:06.615 --> 00:08:07.991
That's another thing.

00:08:07.991 --> 00:08:10.802
One of the biggest focuses for me

00:08:10.802 --> 00:08:13.246
on these four days was you need

00:08:13.246 --> 00:08:17.413
to put in motion into whatever
you want to accomplish.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:21.431
Accept that motivation is
not going to carry through.

00:08:21.431 --> 00:08:23.137
Motivation, you know,
like, will start you up.

00:08:23.137 --> 00:08:24.208
You're like, "All right,
I'm going to go to the gym.

00:08:24.208 --> 00:08:25.587
I'm going to wake up," and, boom,

00:08:25.587 --> 00:08:26.680
two three days you start to do it,

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:28.212
which has been a problem of mine,

00:08:28.212 --> 00:08:29.217
but you drop out.

00:08:29.217 --> 00:08:32.497
So, there's a part of putting in motion

00:08:32.497 --> 00:08:33.667
everything that you do.

00:08:33.667 --> 00:08:34.500
It's not just like,

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:35.408
"Oh, I got to go to the gym,"

00:08:35.408 --> 00:08:36.308
"Oh, I got to do this,"

00:08:36.308 --> 00:08:37.373
"Oh, I got to do this."

00:08:37.373 --> 00:08:39.483
And it's like this anger and angst

00:08:39.483 --> 00:08:41.191
and discomfort and my whole body right now

00:08:41.191 --> 00:08:43.274
is just like crumbling inside.

00:08:43.274 --> 00:08:44.796
So, being aware of that

00:08:44.796 --> 00:08:46.655
and catching yourself
and catching the language

00:08:46.655 --> 00:08:50.696
that you use, and then from
there, seeing the vision

00:08:50.696 --> 00:08:52.798
of you already accomplishing those things,

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:54.496
which I've never really done.

00:08:54.496 --> 00:08:57.616
Like, so I want to get fit,
whatever that means to me.

00:08:57.616 --> 00:08:59.503
I have to make a clear thing.

00:08:59.503 --> 00:09:01.661
This is what fit means for me.

00:09:01.661 --> 00:09:03.917
On a side note, actually, I've realized

00:09:03.917 --> 00:09:06.217
that I want to think about fitness.

00:09:06.217 --> 00:09:07.559
I want to have more energy.

00:09:07.559 --> 00:09:09.567
I want to have more energy myself.

00:09:09.567 --> 00:09:10.693
I don't want to be tired during the day.

00:09:10.693 --> 00:09:11.953
I don't want to take naps.

00:09:11.953 --> 00:09:13.575
For me to want to do something

00:09:13.575 --> 00:09:16.141
to make a big life change
like the smoking or whatever,

00:09:16.141 --> 00:09:17.870
I need to have enough emotion,

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:19.711
I need to hate it enough,

00:09:19.711 --> 00:09:22.799
I need to have enough angst
in it to be like, that's it.

00:09:22.799 --> 00:09:24.436
I'm quitting this for myself.

00:09:24.436 --> 00:09:26.827
I'm actually making
this change for myself.

00:09:26.827 --> 00:09:28.055
So, it's funny to realize

00:09:28.055 --> 00:09:30.743
that there's this level
of pain that you need

00:09:30.743 --> 00:09:33.261
to experience and there's
a level of discomfort

00:09:33.261 --> 00:09:35.305
you need to feel in
order to make a change.

00:09:35.305 --> 00:09:37.871
I realized in this event
that you can induce that.

00:09:37.871 --> 00:09:39.330
Just as much as I can make myself happy,

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:41.280
I can go, "Yeah, woo!"

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.470
I can go energetic, right?

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:43.455
But I can also bring it down.

00:09:43.455 --> 00:09:46.249
So, I'm in control of my body.

00:09:46.249 --> 00:09:47.604
So, you can create these emotions

00:09:47.604 --> 00:09:48.760
if you want to make a change.

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:50.843
So, if you feel like, you know,
I'm not happy with my body.

00:09:50.843 --> 00:09:52.073
I'm not happy with this.

00:09:52.073 --> 00:09:53.357
You start to go to the gym.

00:09:53.357 --> 00:09:55.597
January, New Year's resolution, whatever.

00:09:55.597 --> 00:09:57.258
You start going, you drop out.

00:09:57.258 --> 00:09:58.755
And you hate yourself,
and you hate yourself

00:09:58.755 --> 00:10:00.456
and you start to eat more and do whatever.

00:10:00.456 --> 00:10:02.248
Whatever, everybody has their own cycles.

00:10:02.248 --> 00:10:03.312
I have my cycles.

00:10:03.312 --> 00:10:04.822
It's being like, you know what?

00:10:04.822 --> 00:10:06.105
This is not enough.

00:10:06.105 --> 00:10:09.350
Now, let me picture what the
worst case scenarios are.

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:10.319
In five or ten years,

00:10:10.319 --> 00:10:11.451
if I can continue doing this,

00:10:11.451 --> 00:10:14.028
what's my life going to be like?

00:10:14.028 --> 00:10:14.861
How's it going to look?

00:10:14.861 --> 00:10:15.694
Am I going to be happy?

00:10:15.694 --> 00:10:17.022
And you start to feel the pain for that.

00:10:17.022 --> 00:10:18.388
And you're like, Jesus, you know?

00:10:18.388 --> 00:10:20.395
Excuse me, you know?

00:10:20.395 --> 00:10:24.193
In five or ten years, you
know, your loved one left you.

00:10:24.193 --> 00:10:26.468
Maybe you're thinking you're battling with

00:10:26.468 --> 00:10:28.531
is you're not happy with your career.

00:10:28.531 --> 00:10:30.597
You're coming home and
then all your family

00:10:30.597 --> 00:10:33.180
who love you very much,
your friends, whatever,

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:35.178
your next door neighbor,
whoever cares about you

00:10:35.178 --> 00:10:37.464
and your life and they're
seeing you unhappy

00:10:37.464 --> 00:10:38.735
and you start to suck them in.

00:10:38.735 --> 00:10:39.756
And they start to pull back.

00:10:39.756 --> 00:10:43.082
In five or ten years, you imagine
yourself being left alone.

00:10:43.082 --> 00:10:45.057
Is that enough to make
a change in your life.

00:10:45.057 --> 00:10:46.520
And so for me, there's a bunch of moments

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:48.580
where I've experienced deep emotion,

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.229
just crying for my soul,

00:10:50.229 --> 00:10:52.460
just being in discomfort and pain,

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:55.086
but it was a good thing because I saw

00:10:55.086 --> 00:10:56.779
the light at the end.

00:10:56.779 --> 00:10:57.988
Tony pointed this out.

00:10:57.988 --> 00:10:58.965
He mentioned that he hates

00:10:58.965 --> 00:11:01.208
being called "motivational speaker."

00:11:01.208 --> 00:11:03.187
Motivation is not enough.

00:11:03.187 --> 00:11:04.482
You need to create plans.

00:11:04.482 --> 00:11:05.589
You need to create strategies.

00:11:05.589 --> 00:11:08.232
You need to break bad behaviors.

00:11:08.232 --> 00:11:10.862
You need to break those things

00:11:10.862 --> 00:11:12.372
that you fall into patterns of.

00:11:12.372 --> 00:11:13.632
So, it's like you coming home,

00:11:13.632 --> 00:11:15.174
you grabbing a beer and
every time you think

00:11:15.174 --> 00:11:17.016
of coming home, you're opening that fridge

00:11:17.016 --> 00:11:18.099
and you grabbing that beer.

00:11:18.099 --> 00:11:19.278
So, you got to cut those bad behaviors

00:11:19.278 --> 00:11:21.026
and cut those patterns and whatever.

00:11:21.026 --> 00:11:22.717
You're hitting the snooze button,

00:11:22.717 --> 00:11:24.050
you're sleeping in late, whatever.

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:27.016
So, emotion is important
to give you enough pain

00:11:27.016 --> 00:11:29.155
to make the change.

00:11:29.155 --> 00:11:30.946
And then you got to create a plan.

00:11:30.946 --> 00:11:31.947
You got to create a strategy.

00:11:31.947 --> 00:11:33.588
I hate this thing.

00:11:33.588 --> 00:11:34.517
Why do I want to change it?

00:11:34.517 --> 00:11:35.586
Why is it important to me?

00:11:35.586 --> 00:11:36.921
Okay, how do I make it

00:11:36.921 --> 00:11:40.327
and accept that you're
not going to necessarily

00:11:40.327 --> 00:11:42.554
always wake up every morning and like,

00:11:42.554 --> 00:11:44.455
all right, I got to go to
the gym, blah blah blah.

00:11:44.455 --> 00:11:48.477
But, if you focus on the
emotion of why I do this

00:11:48.477 --> 00:11:50.490
where I'm headed and you
see yourself down there,

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:52.117
you see yourself in that success

00:11:52.117 --> 00:11:53.875
in five or ten years, you're celebrating

00:11:53.875 --> 00:11:55.251
with your friends and you're happy.

00:11:55.251 --> 00:11:57.091
You have that house or whatever it is

00:11:57.091 --> 00:12:00.121
that you want, then that can be enough.

00:12:00.121 --> 00:12:03.138
It's an incredible adventure.

00:12:03.138 --> 00:12:03.971
It's funny.

00:12:03.971 --> 00:12:05.078
I think even if you're not open-minded

00:12:05.078 --> 00:12:08.497
and you go to it, you get
sucked in to the energy.

00:12:08.497 --> 00:12:12.497
You get sucked in to the
raw power of the event.

00:12:13.681 --> 00:12:15.145
Just be open-minded

00:12:15.145 --> 00:12:18.553
and go with a sense of
wonder and curiosity.

00:12:18.553 --> 00:12:20.059
And whatever happens at the end, you know,

00:12:20.059 --> 00:12:23.759
I'm sure, you know, it seemed
when they were talking about

00:12:23.759 --> 00:12:24.617
the things that they learned,

00:12:24.617 --> 00:12:25.884
it seems like it's all
a little bit different,

00:12:25.884 --> 00:12:26.810
it's all interpretations.

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:27.921
So, whatever you learn,

00:12:27.921 --> 00:12:28.835
it could be completely different

00:12:28.835 --> 00:12:32.027
from what I'm saying right now.

00:12:32.027 --> 00:12:34.646
But, yeah, it's something
you don't really want

00:12:34.646 --> 00:12:35.529
to miss out on.

00:12:35.529 --> 00:12:38.200
It's something that's going to...

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:39.907
You know, I don't want to
say "change your life".

00:12:39.907 --> 00:12:40.778
That's one of those things

00:12:40.778 --> 00:12:41.611
that they were talking about.

00:12:41.611 --> 00:12:43.298
You grow, you can't change.

00:12:43.298 --> 00:12:45.019
You just bring out the beauty inside you.

00:12:45.019 --> 00:12:46.871
Bring out the happiness inside you

00:12:46.871 --> 00:12:49.827
and you believe that
you deserve it, right?

00:12:49.827 --> 00:12:51.464
So, I'm not going to say
you're going to go there

00:12:51.464 --> 00:12:54.180
and you're going to change,
but you're going to grow.

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:56.351
And I think that if you ever want

00:12:56.351 --> 00:12:57.864
to improve your life,
the important thing is

00:12:57.864 --> 00:12:59.733
that you got to invest in yourself.

00:12:59.733 --> 00:13:02.190
And so this event blew me away.

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:03.467
Blew me away.

00:13:03.467 --> 00:13:04.645
And I'm really grateful for that.

00:13:04.645 --> 00:13:06.136
I would come back to this event next year

00:13:06.136 --> 00:13:07.727
and I'll bring my family, my brother.

00:13:07.727 --> 00:13:09.591
I'll bring my fianceé, Rosanna.

00:13:09.591 --> 00:13:10.746
Just for them to go.

00:13:10.746 --> 00:13:12.144
Not because they're not perfect.

00:13:12.144 --> 00:13:14.188
It's not about that.

00:13:14.188 --> 00:13:16.512
But it's ust so ...

00:13:16.512 --> 00:13:18.457
It's so overwhelming and beautiful

00:13:18.457 --> 00:13:20.707
that just being around that

00:13:22.071 --> 00:13:24.906
is just worth it in itself.

00:13:24.906 --> 00:13:25.786
- [Evan] You come back next year,

00:13:25.786 --> 00:13:27.487
it'll be with Rosanna, your wife.

00:13:27.487 --> 00:13:28.746
- Yeah. It will be.

00:13:28.746 --> 00:13:30.961
I'm getting married ...

00:13:30.961 --> 00:13:31.794
Oh, thank you.

00:13:31.794 --> 00:13:34.725
We're getting married on ...

00:13:34.725 --> 00:13:35.558
In September.

00:13:35.558 --> 00:13:37.276
Yeah, getting married in September.

00:13:37.276 --> 00:13:38.909
Got to plan a honeymoon.

00:13:38.909 --> 00:13:40.250
Maybe Evan's going to
pay for the honeymoon.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:41.583
I don't know.

00:13:41.583 --> 00:13:43.500
We'll discuss it later.

00:13:47.494 --> 00:13:49.422
(laughing)

00:13:49.422 --> 00:13:51.264
- [Alex] What's so funny, Evan?

00:13:51.264 --> 00:13:52.560
- [Evan] Edwin is there as well.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.393
What did you think, Edwin?

00:13:53.393 --> 00:13:55.535
What did you learn?
What are you take away?

00:13:55.535 --> 00:13:56.882
- I think the energy level

00:13:56.882 --> 00:13:59.256
that is expected of us is something

00:13:59.256 --> 00:14:01.006
that I'm taking away.

00:14:02.067 --> 00:14:05.137
Emotionally, I went up and down a lot.

00:14:05.137 --> 00:14:09.057
Physically, I can't believe
I have that much energy.

00:14:09.057 --> 00:14:13.224
I think most of it is knowing
what the standard is, now

00:14:14.122 --> 00:14:17.185
and how low we were before.

00:14:17.185 --> 00:14:18.975
Yeah, that's the biggest
thing I've learned.

00:14:18.975 --> 00:14:20.947
- So, what did I learn?

00:14:20.947 --> 00:14:22.533
What did I learn from this?

00:14:22.533 --> 00:14:24.436
So, I came to this

00:14:24.436 --> 00:14:26.311
because we've done a lot of content

00:14:26.311 --> 00:14:28.066
on a lot of different successful people,

00:14:28.066 --> 00:14:29.192
and I was never really interested

00:14:29.192 --> 00:14:31.707
in going to see any of them live,

00:14:31.707 --> 00:14:33.724
but I felt with Tony there
would be a different experience.

00:14:33.724 --> 00:14:35.597
I told these guys that earlier.

00:14:35.597 --> 00:14:37.799
But, as much as I love Gary V

00:14:37.799 --> 00:14:41.584
or any of these speakers,
I've seen their full events

00:14:41.584 --> 00:14:42.764
and I don't feel like the vibe

00:14:42.764 --> 00:14:45.305
is that amazing that you need to be there

00:14:45.305 --> 00:14:47.493
versus people who just watch video.

00:14:47.493 --> 00:14:51.160
And I wanted to see if
Tony would be different

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:53.191
because I've consumed
a lot of Tony content.

00:14:53.191 --> 00:14:55.624
A lot of the stuff he talked about,

00:14:55.624 --> 00:14:57.817
the content I never really heard before,

00:14:57.817 --> 00:14:58.979
and so I wasn't taking ...

00:14:58.979 --> 00:15:00.968
I wasn't filling up the notebook,

00:15:00.968 --> 00:15:02.724
but I wanted to experience it.

00:15:02.724 --> 00:15:06.342
And there's also a lot
that you are not ready

00:15:06.342 --> 00:15:08.135
for when you first go.

00:15:08.135 --> 00:15:10.051
- No, it so unexpected.

00:15:10.051 --> 00:15:12.519
- No matter what you
think is going to happen,

00:15:12.519 --> 00:15:14.476
it's going to get crazier.

00:15:14.476 --> 00:15:17.825
I haven't cried as much
in the past four days

00:15:17.825 --> 00:15:20.530
as I have in maybe my life.

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:21.363
I don't know.

00:15:21.363 --> 00:15:22.423
That was crazy.

00:15:22.423 --> 00:15:25.173
Both happy crying and sad crying.

00:15:27.711 --> 00:15:29.029
And you can't really explain it.

00:15:29.029 --> 00:15:30.509
You got to show up and do it.

00:15:30.509 --> 00:15:33.383
One thing that I learned
that was really interesting

00:15:33.383 --> 00:15:36.049
for me was the impact of my parents.

00:15:36.049 --> 00:15:38.848
And they're on my wall at my office

00:15:38.848 --> 00:15:40.052
and Believe came from them.

00:15:40.052 --> 00:15:41.564
They always told me I
was really a Carmichael.

00:15:41.564 --> 00:15:43.076
I could do anything I wanted.

00:15:43.076 --> 00:15:44.198
That's why they're up there

00:15:44.198 --> 00:15:45.968
and the source of Believe is them, too.

00:15:45.968 --> 00:15:47.713
But one interesting thing that came out

00:15:47.713 --> 00:15:50.975
where I realized that the
need to do something important

00:15:50.975 --> 00:15:54.847
and the drive to make a
difference also comes from my mom.

00:15:54.847 --> 00:15:57.045
One of my earlier memories.

00:15:57.045 --> 00:15:59.041
I was, like, eight years old

00:15:59.041 --> 00:16:02.343
and I created this little family newspaper

00:16:02.343 --> 00:16:03.585
and I decided I was
going to make a newspaper

00:16:03.585 --> 00:16:05.113
for the family because we always got

00:16:05.113 --> 00:16:06.502
The Toronto Star delivered.

00:16:06.502 --> 00:16:08.671
I wanted our own family newspaper.

00:16:08.671 --> 00:16:09.913
And I interviewed my mom

00:16:09.913 --> 00:16:14.615
and I asked her why she wanted
to do what she wanted to do.

00:16:14.615 --> 00:16:17.028
So, she was a lawyer and I asked her,

00:16:17.028 --> 00:16:18.046
"Why did you want to be a lawyer?"

00:16:18.046 --> 00:16:20.331
And she corrected me, you know,

00:16:20.331 --> 00:16:22.067
eight-year-old Evan, and said,

00:16:22.067 --> 00:16:24.227
"I don't want to be just a lawyer.

00:16:24.227 --> 00:16:27.122
I want to be a constitutional lawyer."

00:16:27.122 --> 00:16:28.122
And she said

00:16:29.922 --> 00:16:31.461
that she wanted to be
a constitutional lawyer

00:16:31.461 --> 00:16:34.336
because those are the
people who change the laws.

00:16:34.336 --> 00:16:36.392
They were the ones who went
and wrote the new laws,

00:16:36.392 --> 00:16:38.193
and not just living

00:16:38.193 --> 00:16:41.151
within the law system,
but creating new better,

00:16:41.151 --> 00:16:43.318
more fair, more just laws.

00:16:44.414 --> 00:16:46.065
And that's what she wanted to do.

00:16:46.065 --> 00:16:48.480
And I remember thinking,
yeah, I like that.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.068
I want to do something important too.

00:16:50.068 --> 00:16:51.370
I want to have an impact, too.

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:52.502
I want to do something big.

00:16:52.502 --> 00:16:55.405
And I just realized
this weekend that's kind

00:16:55.405 --> 00:16:58.673
of the source of me wanting
to do a lot of big things

00:16:58.673 --> 00:17:01.162
and not just believing in people,

00:17:01.162 --> 00:17:02.371
but doing it in a big way.

00:17:02.371 --> 00:17:05.130
So, I'm going to try to see
what I can find one of those ...

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:07.752
If I can find that old
copy of that newspaper,

00:17:07.752 --> 00:17:09.758
that would be pretty cool.

00:17:09.758 --> 00:17:11.113
