Really crazy hot and
bright in LA, this trip.

00:20:22.844 --> 00:20:23.677
I love it.

00:20:23.677 --> 00:20:25.892
Walking down the street,
come across this place.

00:20:25.892 --> 00:20:26.907
Pavilions.

00:20:26.907 --> 00:20:28.543
Grocery store.

00:20:28.543 --> 00:20:31.526
Got to get some breakfast to
maybe load up for the day.

00:20:31.526 --> 00:20:32.359
Here we go.

00:20:32.359 --> 00:20:33.392
All right. I'm done.

00:20:33.392 --> 00:20:34.779
You guys want to see what I bought?

00:20:34.779 --> 00:20:36.696
I've got a veggie tray.

00:20:38.752 --> 00:20:42.002
I've got roasted and salted mixed nuts.

00:20:43.517 --> 00:20:45.684
I have a thing of bananas.

00:20:46.723 --> 00:20:47.778
That's what I'm going to eat.

00:20:47.778 --> 00:20:49.012
I'm sure Nina's really laughing

00:20:49.012 --> 00:20:52.482
at this part of my product
selection, but it's healthy,

00:20:52.482 --> 00:20:53.604
it sticks to the diet,

00:20:53.604 --> 00:20:55.489
and I'm going to enjoy it.

00:20:55.489 --> 00:20:58.252
(Latino music)

00:20:58.252 --> 00:21:01.755
So, I've decided to stop
off at Peet's Coffee.

00:21:01.755 --> 00:21:02.877
I told Nina.

00:21:02.877 --> 00:21:03.771
She freaked out.

00:21:03.771 --> 00:21:05.733
It's not coffee, it's herbal tea.

00:21:05.733 --> 00:21:07.768
Africa Rooibos something.

00:21:07.768 --> 00:21:08.844
It's actually pretty good.

00:21:08.844 --> 00:21:09.696
Got some work done.

00:21:09.696 --> 00:21:12.412
Ate my veggies and now it's time

00:21:12.412 --> 00:21:15.402
to go meet Mr. Brian Grazer

00:21:15.402 --> 00:21:18.022
and see what he wants to talk about.

00:21:18.022 --> 00:21:18.933
I'm excited.

00:21:18.933 --> 00:21:21.063
All right, well, that was fun.

00:21:21.063 --> 00:21:23.224
We chatted for an hour,

00:21:23.224 --> 00:21:25.601
which seemed to go really quickly.

00:21:25.601 --> 00:21:26.811
He's a pretty cool guy.

00:21:26.811 --> 00:21:27.644
Pretty chill.

00:21:27.644 --> 00:21:29.431
I didn't even know why we were meeting.

00:21:29.431 --> 00:21:30.957
And he has an interesting story

00:21:30.957 --> 00:21:33.349
where he likes to find people

00:21:33.349 --> 00:21:34.671
that he finds interesting

00:21:34.671 --> 00:21:36.693
and have conversations with them.

00:21:36.693 --> 00:21:38.641
And so he just wanted to meet with me

00:21:38.641 --> 00:21:41.122
and what he said was he
loved the Top 10 Rules,

00:21:41.122 --> 00:21:43.181
videos that we put together.

00:21:43.181 --> 00:21:47.335
He had a request for
one to add to the list.

00:21:47.335 --> 00:21:49.861
So, we're going to be making one for him.

00:21:49.861 --> 00:21:52.923
Maybe one for his son, too,
which will be intereting.

00:21:52.923 --> 00:21:54.129
He just wanted to know the story.

00:21:54.129 --> 00:21:55.267
Why I started it.

00:21:55.267 --> 00:21:58.256
His favorite one was Bruce
Lee, which was interesting.

00:21:58.256 --> 00:22:00.776
It's been a while since
we did anything on Bruce.

00:22:00.776 --> 00:22:02.168
And it was super cool.

00:22:02.168 --> 00:22:05.053
It's good to know that the
videos are being watched.

00:22:05.053 --> 00:22:08.053
It's always great to see
people loving the videos

00:22:08.053 --> 00:22:10.672
and having an impact by watching them,

00:22:10.672 --> 00:22:12.820
and looking forward to
new ones coming out.

00:22:12.820 --> 00:22:16.403
So, stay tuned for his
request of a Top 10.

00:22:18.311 --> 00:22:19.878
And now it's ...

00:22:19.878 --> 00:22:24.398
What, I got 45 mintues
to meet with Louis Howes.

00:22:24.398 --> 00:22:27.788
He's another fellow YouTuber,
and he's a podcaster.

00:22:27.788 --> 00:22:29.744
I had him on my channel a while ago.

00:22:29.744 --> 00:22:30.994
And, that's it.

00:22:32.368 --> 00:22:33.314
I'm still feeling full

00:22:33.314 --> 00:22:36.838
from those vegetables, so, pretty good.

00:22:36.838 --> 00:22:38.916
Sticking to the diet so far.

00:22:38.916 --> 00:22:40.499
Day two, yeah.

00:22:40.499 --> 00:22:42.999
(light music)

00:22:44.626 --> 00:22:46.772
All right, I'm at Louis' place.

00:22:46.772 --> 00:22:47.933
Let's do it.

00:22:47.933 --> 00:22:49.147
- What is up everyone?

00:22:49.147 --> 00:22:50.133
I'm Louis Howes here.

00:22:50.133 --> 00:22:52.495
Very excited about this interview.

00:22:52.495 --> 00:22:54.145
We've got Evan Carmichael in the house.

00:22:54.145 --> 00:22:55.357
What's up, brother?
- I'm good, man.

00:22:55.357 --> 00:22:56.657
What is it, right hand to left?

00:22:56.657 --> 00:22:58.379
- Make it awkward.

00:22:58.379 --> 00:22:59.426
- All right, just got out.

00:22:59.426 --> 00:23:00.544
That was a fun session.

00:23:00.544 --> 00:23:03.396
Louis' second hangout ever.

00:23:03.396 --> 00:23:05.635
The last one we did was
three or four years ago.

00:23:05.635 --> 00:23:06.535
So, it was good.

00:23:06.535 --> 00:23:07.535
I showed him how to do it.

00:23:07.535 --> 00:23:11.942
We had some live questions,
great audience and a great guy.

00:23:11.942 --> 00:23:15.215
And apparantly he's coming
to Toronto some point soon.

00:23:15.215 --> 00:23:16.923
September, something like that.

00:23:16.923 --> 00:23:20.193
So, we'll maybe plan something
else when he comes up.

00:23:20.193 --> 00:23:23.430
So, I'm going to head
back to Beverly Hills,

00:23:23.430 --> 00:23:26.178
into the coffee shop, get
a little bit of work done

00:23:26.178 --> 00:23:29.091
and then prepare to meet some fans.

00:23:29.091 --> 00:23:30.926
I love meeting fans when I travel.

00:23:30.926 --> 00:23:35.332
So, we'll see who shows up,
make a video and I'm pumped.

00:23:35.332 --> 00:23:36.494
Let's do it.

00:23:36.494 --> 00:23:38.994
(light music)

00:23:40.441 --> 00:23:41.527
What's up, LA?

00:23:41.527 --> 00:23:44.655
(everyone cheers)

00:23:44.655 --> 00:23:46.256
So we met some fans,

00:23:46.256 --> 00:23:48.098
and before people start kicking off,

00:23:48.098 --> 00:23:49.763
I wanted to pass around the camera.

00:23:49.763 --> 00:23:51.886
They're going to introduce themselves,

00:23:51.886 --> 00:23:54.469
what they do, and what their one word is.

00:23:54.469 --> 00:23:56.184
He's going first because
his parking's running out.

00:23:56.184 --> 00:24:00.416
- I'm Brian, I'm an investor
and my one word is "invest".

00:24:00.416 --> 00:24:01.887
- Hi, I'm Lalaine Lao

00:24:01.887 --> 00:24:03.982
and my company's Access A T,

00:24:03.982 --> 00:24:07.408
eco-friendly t-shirts
and my word is "believe".

00:24:07.408 --> 00:24:08.252
- Hi, I'm Arman.

00:24:08.252 --> 00:24:09.659
I'm the founder of Swab Lube.

00:24:09.659 --> 00:24:11.388
My one word is "persistence".

00:24:11.388 --> 00:24:13.953
- Hi, my name's Ed Reyes.

00:24:13.953 --> 00:24:15.286
I'm 2017 nominee

00:24:16.288 --> 00:24:19.148
for Man of the Year for
Leukemia Lymphoma Society.

00:24:19.148 --> 00:24:22.315
My one word is "hero" #imaherobeahero.

00:24:23.236 --> 00:24:26.492
- Hello, my name is
Kenisha, Chosen Culture.

00:24:26.492 --> 00:24:28.733
I'm a life coach also with Caber Group

00:24:28.733 --> 00:24:30.670
and my one word is "love".

00:24:30.670 --> 00:24:32.825
- What's up Believe Nation,
this is Devon Trish.

00:24:32.825 --> 00:24:33.825
I'm a Virgo.

00:24:36.087 --> 00:24:36.920
I'm an actor.

00:24:36.920 --> 00:24:38.001
My one word, I'm still working on it.

00:24:38.001 --> 00:24:39.500
- Hi, I'm Skylar Ojeda.

00:24:39.500 --> 00:24:42.380
I'm a writer and I would say
my one word is also "love".

00:24:42.380 --> 00:24:45.216
- Hi, my name's Jonathan Chu

00:24:45.216 --> 00:24:48.243
and I work at Disney Imagineering

00:24:48.243 --> 00:24:51.533
and I also started a
company called Choose Joy,

00:24:51.533 --> 00:24:53.670
based off of our last name.

00:24:53.670 --> 00:24:56.320
So, my one word is "hope".

00:24:56.320 --> 00:24:59.430
- Hello, I'm Mandy Chu, also a founder

00:24:59.430 --> 00:25:02.739
of Choose Joy and my one
word is "expression".

00:25:02.739 --> 00:25:04.648
- Hi, I'm Thelma Saunders.

00:25:04.648 --> 00:25:08.514
I am an owner of Thousand
Oaks Fit Body Boot Camp

00:25:08.514 --> 00:25:11.469
and my one word is "flourish".

00:25:11.469 --> 00:25:16.096
- Well, my name's Marilyn and
my word is "perseverance".

00:25:16.096 --> 00:25:18.274
- [Evan] Yeah, all right.

00:25:18.274 --> 00:25:19.607
LA in the house.

00:25:22.257 --> 00:25:23.791
We're going to get back to talking now.

00:25:23.791 --> 00:25:26.034
All right, that was a lot of fun.

00:25:26.034 --> 00:25:28.840
It's always so humbling to meet the fans.

00:25:28.840 --> 00:25:30.210
This was a really good group.

00:25:30.210 --> 00:25:31.776
Man, I love the LA fans.

00:25:31.776 --> 00:25:33.109
That was a really good group.

00:25:33.109 --> 00:25:33.995
People showed up.

00:25:33.995 --> 00:25:35.063
We had a great time.

00:25:35.063 --> 00:25:36.270
I answered a lot of questions,

00:25:36.270 --> 00:25:37.849
got to know some new entrepreneurs.

00:25:37.849 --> 00:25:41.163
People drove from quite a distance, some

00:25:41.163 --> 00:25:43.715
of them to get there.

00:25:43.715 --> 00:25:44.911
It's humbling.

00:25:44.911 --> 00:25:46.411
I started at four.

00:25:47.312 --> 00:25:48.145
Started at four.

00:25:48.145 --> 00:25:51.358
First person came at
four, what time is it now?

00:25:51.358 --> 00:25:52.289
It's eight.

00:25:52.289 --> 00:25:53.122
Four hours.

00:25:53.122 --> 00:25:55.100
One of the things that I find is

00:25:55.100 --> 00:25:58.208
I get more energy with time.

00:25:58.208 --> 00:25:59.829
Like at the beginning,
I still have energy.

00:25:59.829 --> 00:26:02.509
It's good to meet people
and then it picks up.

00:26:02.509 --> 00:26:04.843
I get my energy and now I'm on fire

00:26:04.843 --> 00:26:08.329
and then I'm going to go
home and crash at some point.

00:26:08.329 --> 00:26:10.239
But no, just an amazing experience.

00:26:10.239 --> 00:26:11.575
These guys were awesome

00:26:11.575 --> 00:26:15.566
and looking forward to
coming back again one day.

00:26:15.566 --> 00:26:16.996
See how it goes.

00:26:16.996 --> 00:26:18.448
I'm going to head to
the grocery store again,

00:26:18.448 --> 00:26:20.317
that last place that I was at,

00:26:20.317 --> 00:26:23.856
apparently has a lot of good
feedback and good reviews.

00:26:23.856 --> 00:26:25.765
So, I'm going to see what else I can find

00:26:25.765 --> 00:26:28.848
and head home, see what Nina's up to,

00:26:30.514 --> 00:26:32.579
catch up on work and then get ready

00:26:32.579 --> 00:26:34.496
to fly back to Toronto.

00:26:35.481 --> 00:26:37.981
(peppy music)

00:26:40.313 --> 00:26:41.942
All right, I'm finally back.

00:26:41.942 --> 00:26:43.903
Had a little bit of a
chaotic episode there.

00:26:43.903 --> 00:26:45.274
My visa got cut off.

00:26:45.274 --> 00:26:46.702
I didn't call Visa to let them know

00:26:46.702 --> 00:26:49.457
I was coming to the US
and they cut me off.

00:26:49.457 --> 00:26:51.890
I had to figure out a way
to call and get it fixed.

00:26:51.890 --> 00:26:53.307
But look at this.

00:26:54.259 --> 00:26:55.416
Here's what I bought.

00:26:55.416 --> 00:26:57.333
I bought a green drink.

00:26:59.244 --> 00:27:01.392
Keep on my diet.

00:27:01.392 --> 00:27:04.492
I bought some more nuts for tomorrow.

00:27:04.492 --> 00:27:06.742
I bought one giant avocado.

00:27:08.764 --> 00:27:13.089
I bought another veggie tray
that I can eat right now

00:27:13.089 --> 00:27:15.360
and, Nina's going to love this,

00:27:15.360 --> 00:27:18.027
I bought green beans and onions.

00:27:20.365 --> 00:27:21.317
I thought they were mushrooms.

00:27:21.317 --> 00:27:23.895
Onions and mushrooms
that I'm going to cook.

00:27:23.895 --> 00:27:26.948
We did zero cooking this entire time.

00:27:26.948 --> 00:27:28.151
Every meal was eaten out.

00:27:28.151 --> 00:27:30.026
Zero cooking, so I'm going to make

00:27:30.026 --> 00:27:32.943
the first cooked meal of this trip.

00:27:36.307 --> 00:27:37.140
Here I go.

00:27:37.140 --> 00:27:40.640
Okay, so I burned the thing I was supposed

00:27:40.640 --> 00:27:43.002
to cook pretty badly.

00:27:43.002 --> 00:27:46.252
I added some water to it and we'll see.

00:27:47.157 --> 00:27:49.574
I miss Nina for many reasons.

00:27:51.814 --> 00:27:55.105
I'm going to relax, eat
the rest of my food,

00:27:55.105 --> 00:27:57.680
watch an episode of Billions
because Nina doesn't like it.

00:27:57.680 --> 00:27:59.598
So, I have a chance to watch it here.

00:27:59.598 --> 00:28:01.126
That's it.
Get ready for bed.

00:28:01.126 --> 00:28:05.209
Wake up tomorrow morning
and head back home, woo!

00:28:06.328 --> 00:28:08.037
I mixed some avocado in with it

00:28:08.037 --> 00:28:10.620
and it's actually not that bad.

00:28:13.575 --> 00:28:14.408
Good night.

00:28:14.408 --> 00:28:15.601
Good morning, good morning, good morning.

00:28:15.601 --> 00:28:16.900
It's the last day.

00:28:16.900 --> 00:28:18.792
I am so excited I get to go home.

00:28:18.792 --> 00:28:19.848
Get to see Nina.

00:28:19.848 --> 00:28:21.449
Last night was interesting.

00:28:21.449 --> 00:28:24.699
I'm a bit lonely which is interesting.

00:28:26.020 --> 00:28:27.817
It's an interesting
different feeling, I think

00:28:27.817 --> 00:28:31.210
from having all of the intense experiences

00:28:31.210 --> 00:28:33.716
over the past number of
days, especially with Nina.

00:28:33.716 --> 00:28:35.993
Have a night just be by myself

00:28:35.993 --> 00:28:39.416
and a morning by myself, I
really, really miss Nina.

00:28:39.416 --> 00:28:40.638
I want to get back.

00:28:40.638 --> 00:28:42.484
I mean, I always miss Nina when I go away,

00:28:42.484 --> 00:28:45.104
but I actually feel loneliness.

00:28:45.104 --> 00:28:46.102
What am I going to do?

00:28:46.102 --> 00:28:47.420
What am I going to do?

00:28:47.420 --> 00:28:48.527
Last night I fell asleep.

00:28:48.527 --> 00:28:52.360
I stayed up late watching
episodes of Billions

00:28:53.431 --> 00:28:55.683
when I was supposed to work.

00:28:55.683 --> 00:28:57.616
I wanted to work.

00:28:57.616 --> 00:29:00.131
But I ended up staying up
watching episodes of Billions.

00:29:00.131 --> 00:29:04.027
So, when I'm lonely, i
veg on TV, apparently.

00:29:04.027 --> 00:29:04.909
Interesting.

00:29:04.909 --> 00:29:07.068
I'm going to get my
Uber, head to the airport

00:29:07.068 --> 00:29:09.042
and go home and see Nina.

00:29:09.042 --> 00:29:10.080
Woo!

00:29:10.080 --> 00:29:12.663
(guitar music)

00:29:36.712 --> 00:29:38.795
All right, I'm done, woo!

00:29:39.641 --> 00:29:40.966
Got naseaous on the plane.

00:29:40.966 --> 00:29:43.665
Fighting a headache from all
the turbulance, up and down.

00:29:43.665 --> 00:29:46.034
But it's good to be back.

00:29:46.034 --> 00:29:46.879
I'm excited.

00:29:46.879 --> 00:29:48.363
Let's go see Nina.

00:29:48.363 --> 00:29:50.640
(music)

00:29:50.640 --> 00:29:51.473
- Hi.

00:29:51.473 --> 00:29:52.306
- [Evan] Long time no see

00:29:52.306 --> 00:29:53.139
- [Nina] Long time no see.

00:29:53.139 --> 00:29:53.972
(kissing)

00:29:53.972 --> 00:29:56.756
- I'm happy to see the wife.

00:29:56.756 --> 00:29:57.696
Okay.

00:29:57.696 --> 00:30:01.226
Well, thank you guys for
joining us on another trip.

00:30:01.226 --> 00:30:03.122
No more trips for a while.

00:30:03.122 --> 00:30:04.606
No more trips for a while.
- Really?

00:30:04.606 --> 00:30:05.939
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:30:06.821 --> 00:30:07.654
- Nina's going

00:30:07.654 --> 00:30:09.462
on a trip by herself.
- No, with you.

00:30:09.462 --> 00:30:11.629
We'll document everything.

00:30:13.049 --> 00:30:15.358
Evan is done traveling for a while.

00:30:15.358 --> 00:30:16.846
- What's while?

00:30:16.846 --> 00:30:18.279
- Like two years.

00:30:18.279 --> 00:30:19.426
- Yeah, right.

00:30:19.426 --> 00:30:21.382
You're going soon.

00:30:21.382 --> 00:30:22.779
- No.

00:30:22.779 --> 00:30:24.478
- You're going to in a couple of months.

00:30:24.478 --> 00:30:26.068
- No.

00:30:26.068 --> 00:30:28.263
- Okay, it was fun, though.

00:30:28.263 --> 00:30:29.846
It was a good trip.

00:30:31.329 --> 00:30:32.970
It was a good trip.

00:30:32.970 --> 00:30:34.356
We learned a lot.

00:30:34.356 --> 00:30:35.792
Met some good people.

00:30:35.792 --> 00:30:36.758
I'm very thankful for the trip

00:30:36.758 --> 00:30:38.733
and it's great to see the wife.

00:30:38.733 --> 00:30:39.667
She's back.

00:30:39.667 --> 00:30:40.794
I'm back.

00:30:40.794 --> 00:30:42.402
We're back together.

00:30:42.402 --> 00:30:44.329
- I came back yesterday.

00:30:44.329 --> 00:30:46.162
I came back yesterday.

00:30:47.245 --> 00:30:48.869
- I got to get some food too.

00:30:48.869 --> 00:30:51.346
Thank you guys for joining us

00:30:51.346 --> 00:30:53.418
- Continue to believe, much love

00:30:53.418 --> 00:30:55.747
and whatever your one word is.

00:30:55.747 --> 00:30:57.839
- And we'll see you soon.

00:30:57.839 --> 00:31:00.172
(swooshing)

